SM(528,{"n":"1 Corinthians 1 Continued","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/1 Corinthians 1 Continued.mp3","d":2545.6,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest, serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.12,"To the Church of God, which is at Corinth, to those who are sanctified in Christ Jesus, called to be saints, with all who in every place call on the name of Jesus Christ our Lord, both theirs and ours."],[37.6,"Now this is interesting for a number of reasons."],[42.93,"So he's writing to the the now remember the word church is just the word that's used for the assembly in the Old Testament."],[52.85,"So right So we read about the assembly of Israel."],[55.47,"Moses comes to address the assembly of Israel."],[57.71,"He's got all the people together."],[59.84,"So he's calling the Christian community at Corinth, the Ecclesia in Greek."],[65.94,"The Ecclesia, the assembly of God."],[70.16,"That's not referring to our Protestant friends in the assemblies of God."],[74.8,"Though this is where they got their name."],[76.8,"But already he's made a statement here."],[81.25,"Because the assembly of God in the Old Testament was who?"],[87.01,"Israel was Israel."],[90.23,"It was Israel."],[92.07,"So he's writing to the assembly of God in Corinth."],[95.99,"That's not just the Jews."],[98.8,"That's everybody. That's you are the people of God in Corinth"],[105.22,"I assume there are at least a few Jews in this group."],[108.18,"There are. There are."],[109.22,"But it's not entirely."],[110.52,"In fact, in fact, it may not even be predominantly."],[113.32,"Yeah. There's good reason, as we'll see going on."],[116.06,"So St. Paul starts by addressing who he is."],[120.7,"Now here in this greeting, he's talking about who they are, or at least who they're supposed to be."],[126.92,"Who they are is they are the people of God in Corinth."],[130.73,"Not of Demeter."],[132.39,"But of God, the Holy Trinity."],[137.35,"Which is at Corinth to those who are sanctified in Christ Jesus."],[141.91,"So he says to them, you've been made holy."],[142.79,"You've been purified"],[148.99,"You've been set apart."],[150.85,"You've been set apart from all the other people in Corinth to be a special people by Christ."],[158.85,"Now, as we're going to see, are they acting like that?"],[163.57,"No. But this is who, this is who they are in Christ."],[171.89,"He says, those called to be saints."],[174.37,"Now we throw the word, it's those called to be holy ones."],[179.09,"And Iis, the word there for holy ones, is the word that's used for angels in the Old Testament."],[188.73,"The holy ones in the Old Testament are the angels who are part of God's divine counsel."],[195.69,"So he says, not only are you the people of God, you're the people who belong to Christ."],[204.33,"Christ has set you apart to be this separate and special people."],[209.85,"And you're called to this great destiny."],[215.21,"You're called to not just be holy in the sense of being set apart for the rest of Corinth, but you're called to become, to be glorified."],[224.03,"To share in the life of God."],[228.43,"With all who in every place call in the name of Jesus Christ our Lord."],[232.55,"So you're part of something bigger."],[234.95,"This isn't just true about you."],[237.19,"It's you along with every other Christian community in the whole world."],[243.43,"Okay. So if they hear this, this is automatically going to reorient their thinking."],[248.33,"He's saying, I'm going to speak to you, maybe not as you are, but in terms of who Christ created you to be."],[258.89,"Who you can be, who you should be working to be."],[262.49,"I'm going to address you that way."],[264.49,"I'm going to talk to you that way."],[267.26,"In the hopes that they will live up to."],[271.6,"Live up to this calling that they've received."],[275.28,"Um, little bit of practical application of this right off the bat this is one of the best ways to show love to people."],[284.28,"We tend to treat people the way we think they deserve to be treated."],[289.74,"If someone's rude to us, and acts like a jerk, we treat them like they're a jerk."],[294.7,"If someone causes a problem for us, we treat them like they're a problem."],[298.83,"We sort of judge people and then deal with them accordingly as our judgment."],[305.33,"Or if we like them, then we treat them well, you know."],[308.37,"Um that's not St."],[310.45,"Paul's approach in loving them."],[312.93,"For St. Paul, loving these people means that despite what they may deserve."],[319.9,"He's going to treat them as they as the people who they should be to help them rise to the occasion."],[327.82,"And he's doing that because, of course, St."],[330.86,"Paul didn't get what he deserved when he stood before Christ after having gone around murdering Christians."],[338.24,"He was not treated the way he deserved."],[341.04,"This this is probably just a grammatical thing, but both theirs and ours, does that refer to Lord?"],[349.36,"I'm not sure who the they and the uh there's an theirs and ours is referring to it."],[355.36,"He's he's talking about all the communities."],[357.92,"Okay. Ours would be the ones that St."],[360.58,"Paul was involved with."],[362.1,"Okay Oh, I see."],[365.02,"Sorry, and then the ones that he wasn't."],[367.74,"So he's referring to when he's saying you're part of the whole, all these communities are connected, it's everybody."],[374.23,"He's saying, I'm not saying you're connected to all the other churches I planted."],[379.19,"He's saying you're connected to all of them, whether I was involved or not."],[384.77,"Because this isn't the church of Paul."],[387.01,"Okay, so that is more significant."],[388.83,"Yeah, it's not the first Pauline church of Corinth."],[393.36,"So grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."],[398.32,"As we've seen, this is St."],[400.0,"Paul's normal way of talking about the relationship between God the Father and Christ."],[403.6,"about the He talks God the Father and Lord Jesus Christ."],[413.18,"In tandem together all the time."],[415.18,"And we're going to see a little later in 1 Corinthians why that's so important."],[421.34,"We're going to find out where where he gets that phrase that he uses all the time."],[425.82,"But I'll just leave that as a tease until we get there."],[428.78,"And it's going to you by Christ Jesus, that you are enriched in everything by him in all utterance and all knowledge, even as the testimony of Christ was confirmed in you."],[448.38,"So that you come short in no gift, eagerly waiting for the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ, who will also confirm you to the end, that you may be blameless b blameless in the day of our Lord Jesus Christ."],[461.14,"God is faithful, by whom you were called into the fellowship of his Son, Jesus Christ our Lord."],[466.82,"Okay, that's all one big sentence in Greek."],[469.54,"That's all I went ahead and went through it."],[472.66,"We we uh English has if you put more than a couple of clauses, English sentences fall apart."],[481.22,"That's not true in Greek and Latin."],[484.26,"Yeah. In uh you can have words that go on for pages in German."],[487.94,"Yeah. But uh in in Latin as a as an example, in uh Caesar's conquest of Gaul. uh, if you get the Loeb Latin version, he has a sentence that goes on for 17 pages"],[502.14,"And the last word is the subject."],[507.18,"But uh that's why I had trouble with that."],[509.82,"But St. Paul sometimes gives him a run for his money in Greek."],[513.66,"Um, because in Greek you can just keep latching on clause after clause after clause and embedding them inside each other."],[519.98,"So that's why you get sometimes long sentences like this with St."],[523.34,"Paul. But so working through it a little more slowly."],[528.58,"Notice again, he starts by saying that he constantly thanks God concerning them."],[535.82,"So again, he's not treating them as a problem, he's gonna go into the problems."],[539.74,"'s not But he treating us as a problem."],[539.78,"It's not that he doesn't know."],[539.9,"He gives thanks for them"],[545.3,"Notice, though, what all this describes, he's giving thanks for."],[549.86,"He's giving thanks for the grace which was given to them."],[553.94,"He's giving thanks for all the things that were given to them."],[558.5,"So reminding them in the process of all the things that were given them."],[562.26,"He's not giving thanks for what they've done with those things necessarily."],[568.26,"But he's thank he's saying he thanks God that they have everything they need to remind them, hey, you have everything you need."],[579.26,"So the grace of God was given to them by Christ Jesus, that you were enriched in everything by Him, in all utterance and all knowledge."],[588.12,"So they've been taught the gospel."],[590.62,"There's not anything that they don't know."],[592.54,"There's not like information about the gospel that they don't have."],[597.58,"Even as the testimony of Christ was confirmed in you."],[601.08,"So what does that mean?"],[602.84,"The testimony of Christ would be the gospel, it being confirmed in them would likely be a reference to their baptism."],[609.82,"So you were you were baptized, you're brought into the church ritually."],[613.27,"Sacramentally. So that you come short in no gift."],[619.33,"So you've received gifts from the Holy Spirit."],[623.23,"All this is true of you."],[624.51,"you. So that come short no gift, eagerly waiting for the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ"],[631.91,"Now notice we're so used to in English talking about Christ's return."],[640.29,"Christ's return, which makes it sound like he's going to come back."],[644.13,"Like he went away somewhere."],[647.11,"Like the ascension was him getting released like a balloon and he floated off somewhere."],[653.35,"And now he's gone someplace."],[656.07,"And at some point in the future, he's going to come back down from wherever he. is"],[662.79,"Yeah So, and well, and return, sort of, you know, the English translation deterrent return implies he's departed."],[670.93,"And this actually, and I know I always say it's an oversimplification, but I've gotten away with saying it many times, so I'll say it again."],[679.41,"This actually plays out in Western Christian theology in the sense that in Roman Catholicism, Christ has a vicar."],[690.09,"The bishop of Rome."],[692.89,"So Christ departs, he leaves Saint Peter in charge."],[699.87,"And then Saint Peter appoints the next and the next and the next."],[704.32,"And so uh Christ is gone somewhere, but he has invested this particular person with power and abilities to sort of govern the church in his stead."],[717.74,"In uh most Protestant thinking, Christ has departed and he's left a book."],[727.56,"He's left a book."],[728.68,"And so we can read about him and learn about him and debate about him."],[734.1,"And have our theological discussions and theologize about him."],[737.96,"But he's someplace."],[742.24,"And until he returns, we've got the book."],[746.05,"In the Orthodox understanding, uh, and in St."],[750.05,"Paul's understanding, I don't think coincidentally, Christ didn't go anywhere."],[752.85,"We confess this every single liturgy"],[760.01,"Christ is in our midst."],[762.65,"He is and ever shall be."],[764.33,"When we gather, Christ is here with us."],[767.61,"Christ comes to us and offers himself to us in the Eucharist."],[772.57,"Right before he ascends in St."],[774.49,"Matthew's gospel, right before he ascends into heaven, he says, Lo, I am with you always, even until the end of the age."],[781.77,"So right before he quote unquote leaves, he says, I'm always going to be with you, meaning he's not leaving."],[786.17,"'s not leaving. He"],[789.71,"Um, and so when Saint Paul talks about Christ's quote unquote return, he tends to use language like here, where Christ is revealed."],[802.67,"Or he refers to Christ's glorious appearing, that he appears."],[807.63,"The Greek word parousia, that's what's usually translated return, doesn't mean return, it means presence."],[815.41,"So a literal translation of that would be when Christ is present again."],[819.99,"Which also refers to appearing."],[823.6,"Appearing. So Christ is here with us."],[826.32,"We can't see him and touch his hands the way the apostles could yet."],[831.84,"But the time will come when he will appear to us, when he will be revealed to us."],[837.85,"In the same way that the apostles."],[840.17,"So that's how he talks about this day that's coming."],[845.54,"And so notice he says, eagerly waiting for the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ."],[852.98,"He's about to mention the fact that Christ's revelation is going to bring about the judgment."],[860.9,"So what does it mean to be able to eagerly await Christ appearing?"],[867.7,"You must expect to be okay."],[870.36,"Then it means that you've lived a life where Christ's appearing is going to mean that you're going to be blessed, rewarded, vindicated."],[879.24,"So that's that's what you're expecting."],[881.72,"So St. Paul's saying, you've been given all these things so that, why were you given all these things so that you can eagerly await?"],[888.64,"You don't have to dread it."],[889.44,"You don't have to be afraid of it."],[891.22,"The people out there who are working wickedness who are in sin, they have to be afraid of Christ's return."],[898.98,"You shouldn't. Because you've been given all these things."],[904.67,"Notice who will also confirm you to the end that you may be blameless on the day of our Lord Jesus Christ."],[910.29,"So that's the goal is to be blameless, to stand before Him."],[913.33,"Blameless, pure, returning that language of holiness."],[917.35,"That he used before."],[918.71,"Notice he refers to it as the day of our Lord Jesus Christ."],[922.31,"Why is that important?"],[923.99,"Well, throughout the prophets, the Old Testament prophets. the day of judgment is the day of Yahweh, the day of the Lord"],[934.41,"That's when God is going to come and visit his people, reestablish justice."],[939.23,"Judge the world all through the prophets."],[941.95,"St. Paul just referred to that day as the day of our Lord, the day of our Lord."],[948.52,"Jesus Christ. So this shouldn't be ambiguous."],[954.92,"He just said Jesus is God."],[959.0,"He just said Jesus is Yahweh."],[963.0,"This is one of many examples."],[965.36,"He's also just said God, meaning the Father, and our Lord Jesus Christ."],[973.12,"And he's now said that Jesus is Yahweh."],[975.6,"So what does that mean?"],[977.36,"That means he has the idea of the Holy Trinity in his head."],[981.28,"This is not something that people come up with later and invent."],[991.2,"And over here it says that, you know, his father and the son."],[995.28,"I don't know."],[995.76,"Let's come up with something."],[996.9,"That's not how it works."],[1000.28,"St. Paul already has this in his head."],[1003.4,"He speaks about them separately."],[1005.96,"He clearly identifies both as being Yahweh, the God of the Old Testament."],[1011.16,"He has this concept firmly in mind."],[1014.92,"And so he can then say, after identifying Christ as God, God is faithful, by whom you were called into the fellowship of his Son, Jesus Christ our Lord."],[1025.44,"So now he can talk again separately."],[1029.2,"Verse 10. Now we get to the bad news."],[1034.32,"Now I plead with you, brethren."],[1037.04,"Remember, we saw that he called brethren, he calls them brothers."],[1041.44,"Remember, we saw in Acts already that this was the language that was used to refer to the faithful in different cities as uh St."],[1052.32,"Paul visited them."],[1053.22,"They were the brethren."],[1054.34,"Because there's this whole idea of being part of the family of God"],[1059.57,"So they're brothers and sisters."],[1061.25,"Now I plead with you, brethren, by the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that you all speak the same thing, and that there be no divisions among you, but that you be perfectly joined together in the same mind and in the same judgment."],[1078.29,"So he's heard their bickering."],[1081.75,"There's factions, there's infighting."],[1083.75,"I know that never happens at our church, but there are other churches where things like that happen, where people don't get along."],[1090.79,"Um, and so he's heard about it"],[1093.27,"He says, Listen."],[1095.32,"Now, he's already following that pattern."],[1098.2,"We talked about at the beginning of Romans."],[1100.28,"St. Paul, here in his opening parts of the letter, sort of lays out the themes that he's going to talk about all the way through."],[1107.12,"So we've already seen one of those therefore here."],[1110.3,"Here's who you are, here's what you've been given, here's what you're called to."],[1114.86,"That means, you should all be of one mind."],[1118.96,"You should all be together."],[1120.24,"You should all be on the same page."],[1124.8,"For it's been declared to me concerning you, my brethren, by those of Chloe's household."],[1130.08,"So there's the rat."],[1131.28,"Uh-huh. By those of Chloe's household, that there are contentions among you."],[1139.2,"Now I say this: that each of you says, I am of Paul, or I am of Apollos, or I am of Cephas, or I am of Christ."],[1146.96,"So remember what we said"],[1148.2,"Okay. Remember theirs or ours?"],[1155.88,"Theirs or ours, who played at the church."],[1158.96,"Part of the factions there are they sort of have formed fan clubs around different apostles and preachers and teachers."],[1169.62,"Where one's saying, Oh, well, I'm I'm a follower of Paul, and somebody else is saying, Oh, I'm a follower of Apollos."],[1175.22,"Remember who he met in Acts, who's been preaching."],[1177.7,"Or, you know, I'm a follower."],[1179.34,"rem Remberemember, Kephas is uh Peter, his Aramaic name."],[1184.74,"It's Aramaic for Petros."],[1186.52,"So you say, Oh, I belong, I'm I'm in this faction or that faction."],[1190.6,"Yeah And the really self-righteous ones say, Well, I'm of Christ."],[1194.51,"To try to trump everybody."],[1195.71,"Yeah. Yeah. I remember when I was when I was six or seven, this shows you how how smart I was at six or seven."],[1204.0,"I had learned in Sunday school that uh since I'm Dutch, that our people were descended."],[1209.44,"We're talking about the story of Noah and then the nations afterwards."],[1212.96,"I learned that we were descended from Japheth."],[1216.14,"That the Dutch people."],[1217.5,"And so I went to school and I told one of the other kids, hey, you know what I found out?"],[1221.26,"You know, you know, Noah's sons."],[1222.72,"Ham, Shem, and Japheth."],[1224.24,"I found out our family's descended from Japheth."],[1226.56,"And he said, Well, my family's descended from Noah himself."],[1232.24,"And I was like, man."],[1237.48,"So, so this is that same kind of one upper thing."],[1242.12,"They're trying to bypass it all."],[1244.6,"Um I think this has this has an obvious uh application in our in our contemporary Christian world, not just among, for example, our Protestant friends, where you have churches named after Martin Luther and John Calvin and John Wesley and very various other people in these factions."],[1266.84,"But even within even within the Orthodox Church in any given age, there's this tendency to sort of form these cults of personality around certain teachers and certain figures, certain personalities on ancient faith radio, who sort of is, oh well, this is I'm a fan of you know this person."],[1288.0,"I'm I'm with this person, I'm with that person."],[1290.24,"And then if there are disagreements between those people, you go on the interwebs and you know bicker with you know the devotees of the other person, you know, and bicker back and forth about you know the differences and this kind of thing."],[1303.92,"And and what St."],[1304.8,"Paul is saying is this is destructive."],[1307.49,"This is destructive to the unity of the church."],[1311.17,"This is destructive to the unity of the church, this kind of these kind of fan club factions when they form."],[1320.53,"So he says in uh verse 13, is Christ divided?"],[1325.85,"Was Paul crucified for you?"],[1327.45,"Were you baptized in the name of Paul?"],[1330.15,"So first he says, Is Christ divided?"],[1331.99,"Are there are there little sections?"],[1334.21,"But then more to the point, he says, Was Paul was I crucified for you?"],[1339.03,"Were you baptized into my name?"],[1340.95,"Obviously, no. So you shouldn't be my follower."],[1345.54,"Remember at the very the very first sentence of the letter."],[1348.84,"It's not about him."],[1350.52,"He's someone who was called and then sent on a mission."],[1353.9,"What's important is the person who called him and who sent him."],[1358.24,"So, and this could be asked about any of those distinctions we were just talking about."],[1362.98,"Did this priest or that author, right"],[1367.74,"Die for you."],[1368.78,"No. He says, I thank God that I baptized none of you except Crispus and Gaius."],[1374.46,"We're about to find out that St."],[1375.42,"Paul doesn't have a good memory."],[1376.62,"Yes. I remember that's uh I thank God that I baptized none of you except Crispus and Gaius."],[1382.55,"But this is starting to show us a little bit of the makeup of the Corinthian church, because those are both Roman names."],[1388.77,"Very traditional Roman names."],[1391.73,"Lest anyone should say that I had baptized in my own name."],[1395.03,"So he's saying, look, I'm glad that I only baptized a couple of people."],[1399.11,"So that no one could say I was there trying to make followers."],[1403.33,"Because he's saying, I wasn't trying to do this."],[1405.81,"Yes, I also baptized the household of Stephanus."],[1406.53,"Besides, I do not know whether I baptized any other"],[1413.19,"So you can imagine him dictating this."],[1415.83,"Oh, well, I also baptized."],[1417.59,"Yeah, I also baptized."],[1419.35,"And maybe some other people."],[1420.55,"I don't know."],[1428.79,"But the point being."],[1430.8,"The point being, he didn't go there trying to make followers."],[1433.92,"Uh-huh. I didn't go there to try and have fans."],[1437.36,"Of Paul. That's not why I came."],[1441.52,"For Christ did not send me to baptize, but to preach the gospel."],[1445.04,"Not with wisdom of words, lest the cross of Christ should be made of no effect."],[1449.2,"That's what he means by he did send me to baptize."],[1449.22,"So he didn't send me there to baptize and form a group."],[1454.08,"Because obviously he is baptizing people."],[1456.32,"But remember, uh, when when St."],[1459.44,"John the Forerunner, if we go way back to when we were talking about the gospels, uh St."],[1464.4,"John the Forerunner, part of what he was doing when he was baptizing people in the Jordan was creating this people, this group of followers for Christ."],[1473.25,"So this is what St."],[1474.13,"Paul means when he says he didn't come there to baptize."],[1476.53,"I didn't come there to make my own group of followers."],[1480.13,"He says, I came there to preach the gospel of Christ, which is about Christ, not about me."],[1486.85,"I came to preach the gospel of Christ, and not with wisdom of words, lest the cross of Christ should be made of no effect."],[1495.37,"Meaning, I didn't come to you with brilliant rhetoric again, so that you'd say, Oh, his sermons are so beautiful."],[1503.77,"Oh, Paul, you are the great."],[1506.15,"He didn't come preaching that way again, because that's not what he wanted."],[1512.47,"That's not what he wanted."],[1513.51,"He wanted the focus of the people who were hearing them to be on Christ and his cross, not on him and what a great speaker he was."],[1523.91,"Or how wise he was."],[1526.63,"For the message of the cross is foolishness to those who are perishing."],[1531.03,"But to us who are being saved, it is the power of God."],[1535.35,"Okay So he says, This I've he's got all over the world."],[1540.21,"Preaching this message, preaching about the cross of Christ."],[1543.41,"And to the people out there who are perishing."],[1546.31,"The people there who are on their way to condemnation, the people who are immersed in their sins, who have decided to keep going down that route, it's foolishness to them."],[1554.47,"They laugh at it."],[1555.51,"They say it's ridiculous."],[1556.87,"As they do today."],[1558.13,"They think it's silly."],[1560.69,"They always go back to Acts 17."],[1562.45,"Remember, as soon as you brought up the resurrection."],[1565.63,"In in Athens, all the philosophers went."],[1568.33,"What are you talking about?"],[1569.82,"Laughed him out of the room."],[1571.5,"Or the agra in that case."],[1573.34,"But um, but uh, you say, look, it it's's it's foolishness to them."],[1581.92,"But to those who are being saved, it is the power of God."],[1585.73,"The people who are faithfully following Christ, it's the power of God."],[1590.15,"What does that mean?"],[1591.43,"It's what's changing, it's what's changing your life."],[1595.43,"It's what's giving you all those things I just listed."],[1598.65,"That is what it is for you."],[1600.09,"Again, the message, not the way I preach it."],[1603.71,"But the message itself, Christ himself."],[1607.31,"For it is written, I will destroy the wisdom of the wise and bring to nothing the understanding of the prudent."],[1614.03,"Okay. And uh that's from Isaiah, Isaiah chapter 29."],[1620.43,"Before I talk about that specifically, I'll go on a little further"],[1625.88,"Where is the wise?"],[1627.16,"Where is the scribe?"],[1628.36,"Where is the disputer of this age?"],[1630.68,"Has not God made foolish the wisdom of this world?"],[1634.76,"For since in the wisdom of God the world through wisdom did not know God, it pleased God through the foolishness of the message preached to save those who believe."],[1645.8,"So, again, that's a roundabout sentence."],[1648.64,"But when he's talking about the wisdom of the world, again, this is another thing that points at a Gentile audience."],[1654.74,"In Corinth. Because uh they're not quite the Athenians."],[1659.37,"But wisdom, is what is highly, what is highly prized."],[1662.51,"Remember Philosophia, the love of wisdom"],[1663.96,"Philosophy. This is what he's talking about."],[1671.14,"He said, all of these wise people in the world didn't come to know God through their wisdom."],[1679.7,"But through the foolishness, through the sending, sending St."],[1684.02,"Paul. And remember, I know I talked about this back in Acts, but we have some physical descriptions of Saint Paul."],[1690.74,"Um, and they include the fact that he had an eye condition where they oozed pus all the time, he was bald, he was short, he was bow legged."],[1700.9,"Um remember, on top of all that, he'd been beaten nearly to death several times with rocks, with scourges."],[1709.63,"Um you would not look at this person and find him attractive."],[1714.73,"And he's saying, I didn't come to you and speak with all this flowery rhetoric, that anyone would think of attractive."],[1722.36,"He says, so yeah, here's me, I'm ridiculous."],[1726.36,"Here's me, I'm a fool."],[1728.44,"But this message that I've preached to you, not me, but the message, is what has finally brought you to come to know God."],[1739.2,"And the fact that I'm a fool, and the fact that I'm ridiculous, and the fact that I'm laughable proves that it's not me, but that it's the message, that it's Gods Himelf doing."],[1749.28,"elf. I always thought that this referred to the message its"],[1754.04,"That the idea of that somebody rose from the dead after being crucified and everything was in itself nonsense to speak."],[1766.68,"We'll get to that in a second here."],[1768.28,"And he's not talking about the resurrection here."],[1769.88,"So we got the cross specifically."],[1773.72,"So now in verse 22, for Jews request a sign, and Greeks seek after wisdom."],[1780.3,"So Jews, the Jewish people want to see miracles."],[1785.08,"They want to see things happen."],[1786.77,"We saw that all through, especially in St."],[1789.09,"John's gospel. They're always coming to Jesus and wanting a sign."],[1792.47,"There have never been enough people here"],[1794.09,"What are you going to do now?"],[1795.13,"Because he'd never done enough miracles."],[1798.99,"Show us something new."],[1800.37,"And the Greeks, they're after wisdom."],[1803.0,"They want your philosophical arguments and your speculation and your lofty discourse."],[1808.2,"But we preach Christ crucified."],[1810.2,"So he comes and he preaches Christ crucified."],[1813.72,"He preaches that God himself became a less than dirt poor peasant, and was executed in a humiliating, tortuous way by the Roman authorities."],[1828.36,"That's what I give you"],[1830.05,"You ask for a sign."],[1832.15,"You ask for a miracle, some kind of displayy of power, you ask for some kind of wisdom, some kind of loft argumentation."],[1834.15,"This is what I give you"],[1840.83,"This is what I give you."],[1843.15,"To the Jews, a stumbling block."],[1845.89,"Why is it a stumbling block to the Jews?"],[1848.13,"Well, because pretty much the sign that you weren't really the Messiah is that the Romans crucify you."],[1854.26,"That's what happened to most of the people who showed up claiming to be the Messiah."],[1860.1,"And the rest of them were executed in different ways."],[1862.66,"They were all killed by the Romans."],[1865.08,"So the Jews, as soon as they hear that, they're like, what?"],[1869.77,"What? And to the Greeks, foolishness."],[1875.71,"The Greeks don't know what. to do with any of that"],[1878.63,"Right? Because remember, the gods of the that the Greeks worship are all gods who represent power."],[1890.07,"And their whole belief is that you become like what you worship, which is a true principle that they stumbled upon."],[1898.87,"That's you do become like what you worship."],[1902.31,"But so they worshipped what?"],[1904.31,"Zeus is power."],[1906.73,"Average beauty. They're God."],[1909.93,"Sensuality, wealth. Physical strength."],[1914.31,"Health. Bountiful harvest."],[1917.01,"These are the things they're worshiping."],[1918.29,"These are the things their Gods represent"],[1918.37,"These are the things they're pursuing."],[1922.49,"And you say, Well, what's your God?"],[1924.65,"And you show them Jesus being executed on a cross."],[1931.37,"What? What? We have some early, it's probably late first century, maybe early second century, graffiti, um, of some Romans making fun of a Christian who was in their military unit."],[1947.31,"And they drew a little dood doodle of a man with a donkey head being crucified."],[1954.11,"And then a little doodle of a guy on his knees, and they said, you know, so-and-so worshiping his God."],[1960.77,"So this is what St."],[1961.81,"Paul's talking about when he says. it's foolishness"],[1964.78,"Because to them it's like you want to become like that."],[1970.38,"But to those who are called both Jews and Greeks, Christ, the power of God and the wisdom of God."],[1978.96,"God's power and wisdom is Christ."],[1983.7,"And is being displayed in that cross."],[1987.78,"Because the foolishness of God is wiser than men, and the weakness of God is stronger than men."],[1994.12,"That's something you sort of have to agree with."],[1995.96,"Well, yeah. Yeah."],[1998.97,"But so, yes, he's talking about the message."],[2003.22,"He's talking about. the person who came preaching it"],[2007.1,"But all of this remembers in the context of."],[2010.24,"This is not how you garner a following."],[2013.76,"I didn't come and give the people what they wanted."],[2016.64,"I gave them what they didn't want."],[2020.8,"I didn't come and tell you what you wanted."],[2023.44,"But but what I told you is what you needed to hear."],[2027.9,"It's not that there's a problem with the gospel."],[2031.6,"And so they need to reorient how they're thinking and refocus on Christ."],[2038.72,"Refocus on who Christ is."],[2041.46,"Who offered his life for the life of the world and for its salvation."],[2046.03,"Rather than on. you know, I'm part of this faction, I'm I'm this guy's fan, I'm part of this group"],[2053.43,"Those two mindsets are completely separated."],[2058.07,"For you see your calling, brethren."],[2061.59,"Now notice he just said to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks."],[2065.97,"That call, remember, he's already used that verb about himself."],[2071.15,"So he's saying it's not just me that's called, it's you."],[2074.85,"It's you. You haven't been sent on the same mission, but you're still called."],[2079.03,"So he says, for you see your calling, brethren."],[2081.44,"You see the people around you."],[2082.74,"This means look around while you're hearing this at the gathering."],[2088.1,"That not many wise according to the flesh, not many mighty, not many noble."],[2093.2,"You look around your church, not a lot of wealthy people, not a lot of big strong people, not a lot of learned philosophers."],[2101.86,"That's not who you are."],[2104.58,"But God has chosen the foolish things of the world to put to shame the wise, and God has chosen the weak things of the world to put to shame the things which are mighty, and the base things of the world and the things which are despised, God has chosen, and the things which are not to bring to nothing the things that are, that no flesh should glory in his presence."],[2129.62,"Again, that's one big sentence."],[2132.54,"So he says, Look, you look around, not many of your life, but God, but God has chosen specifically."],[2140.0,"And Saint Paul's including himself in this list."],[2147.65,"So he's chosen people who aren't wise philosophers, who aren't super educated."],[2155.49,"He's chosen the weak things of the world to shame those who are mighty and strong and powerful."],[2160.61,"And the base things of the world which are despised, God has chosen."],[2166.71,"So these are the people who God has chosen."],[2168.63,"That includes you, that includes me."],[2170.57,"St. Paul is saying."],[2171.87,"We've all been chosen by God."],[2173.79,"And the things which are not to bring to nothing the things that are."],[2176.35,"that And what's a reference to?"],[2178.79,"That's actually a reference to God's name."],[2182.95,"It's actually a reference to God's name."],[2185.19,"Because he isn't, Saint Paul isn't, as we mentioned in Romans, St."],[2188.95,"Paul speaks historically."],[2190.31,"He's not just talking about Corinth."],[2192.23,"He's talking about since the beginning of time."],[2195.67,"That this is how God has operated."],[2198.97,"So this is a fundamental difference between Yahweh, the God of Israel, and all of these pagan gods who represent strength and power and wealth and beauty and all these things."],[2209.46,"From the very beginning, go back to the Torah."],[2213.38,"Who does God identify Himself with?"],[2217.3,"Nomads, orphans, the widow, the poor, strangers, slaves."],[2220.42,"In Egypt That's one of the reasons Pharaoh laughs at Moses."],[2227.96,"Why should I what's the God of a bunch of slaves going to do to me?"],[2234.58,"These are the people who all the way through, all the way through, God has identified himself with."],[2242.98,"These are his people."],[2244.36,"And so being one of his people means being like that."],[2248.65,"His very name, the name Yahweh, is a form of the uh Hebrew verb to be, which is Hayar Hava."],[2258.42,"Uh, I won't go into all that, why there's two different versions."],[2261.46,"But uh um it's a form of of that Hebrew word, which is in the third person, and it's in I don't know how much I want to go into this because people are gonna fall asleep while driving listening to this."],[2275.34,"But uh Hebrew Hebrew verbs don't have tenses, uh, really."],[2280.54,"Um we think of verbs in terms of tenses."],[2283.02,"They have what are called binyons, which are uh sort of uh ways in which they function."],[2288.86,"And the name Yahweh is the verb to be in what's called the Hiffilbinion."],[2293.74,"The Hiffilbinion is causative."],[2296.46,"So all that is to say, all the jargon out of the way, God's name Yahweh means he who causes things to be."],[2304.46,"He who causes things to be."],[2306.3,"So that's not only a reference to him as the creator, God's the creator who creates everything, but he's the one who brought Israel into being, which was not a nation."],[2316.9,"There's a bunch of slaves and refugees and nomads from all different ethnicities."],[2321.54,"Once we loop around at the end of the Old Testament, New Testament, go back into the Old Testament, we get to Exodus, we'll talk more about that."],[2328.82,"That just from the text, there are all kinds of Israelites who are not descended from Jacob ethnically."],[2338.58,"But they weren't a nation, God makes them a nation."],[2342.58,"Paul, we already saw in Romans use that same language about the church"],[2342.88,"And St. Which is a bunch of Gentiles, a bunch of Jews, people, Greeks. people from all over, who have now been made one people in Christ"],[2357.47,"So he's deliberately in this list referring them back to who God is in the scriptures at the time, which is our Old Testament, who he's always been."],[2367.55,"He's always identified with the weak, the powerless, the lowly, because he's the one, his identity, he's the one who takes things that aren't, that are nothing, and makes them into something."],[2379.71,"And that's what he's doing with them."],[2382.75,"That's what he's doing with the Corinthians."],[2385.31,"They're nothing. He's making them into something."],[2389.47,"Okay. And God has done all this, according to St."],[2393.39,"Paul, so that no flesh. should glory in his presence"],[2398.21,"He's deliberately identified himself with the lowly and the weak because they can't stand up and be proud about anything."],[2407.51,"They can't stand up and be proud about anything."],[2409.75,"So this is going all the way back."],[2412.39,"Paul's saying, I'm not here for my glory."],[2415.83,"You shouldn't be either."],[2417.19,"None of us are."],[2419.08,"God picked me and he picked you because we're the dregs."],[2423.58,"We're the despised."],[2424.78,"We're the laughed at."],[2425.66,"We're the mocked."],[2426.46,"That's why God picked us."],[2428.14,"Because that's who God's always picked."],[2430.06,"And now he's going to do these powerful things."],[2433.34,"These powerful things among us."],[2436.06,"But of him you are in Christ Jesus, who became for us wisdom from God, and righteousness and sanctification and redemption."],[2444.66,"That is, it is written, he who glories, let him glory in the Lord."],[2449.62,"Christ became for us the wisdom of God."],[2452.67,"So he became wisdom."],[2455.17,"So if you want wisdom, if that's what you want, Greeks."],[2458.15,"You want wisdom, then you need Christ."],[2460.39,"Because he's the wisdom of God."],[2462.68,"Righteousness. There's some Pharisees around there."],[2466.2,"You're all about righteousness."],[2468.34,"You want righteousness to be just, to be pure, then you need Christ, because Christ is the righteousness of God."],[2475.79,"Sanctification. You want to be holy?"],[2477.95,"You want holiness?"],[2478.27,"holiness Christ is the of God."],[2478.67,"He is who you need"],[2484.23,"Redemption. Referring to the forgiveness of sins being bought back."],[2488.79,"Being purchased back from sin."],[2490.79,"That's what you're looking for, speed of reason."],[2492.95,"Then you need Christ because Christ is God's redemption."],[2497.35,"And so, if anyone is going to glory, if anyone is going to boast about anything."],[2503.77,"You need to be boasting about Christ who has done all this for you."],[2508.17,"Not talking about Paul or Apollos or Peter or whoever."],[2513.69,"So this is probably a good place to stop since we're at the end of chapter one."],[2519.05,"We take the introduction."],[2520.17,"So thank you, everybody."],[2523.17,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2530.53,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2535.89,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.12,"lv":2,"h":"1 Corinthians 1:2 - To the church of God at Corinth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:2</b>: \"To the church of God which is at Corinth, to those sanctified in Christ Jesus, called to be saints, with all who in every place call on the name of Jesus Christ our Lord, both theirs and ours\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><i>Church</i> = word for the <b>assembly</b> in the OT</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses addresses the <b>assembly of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ecclesia</b> = assembly of God (Protestant \"Assemblies of God\" got name here)</li><li class=\"d0\">Already a <b>statement</b>: assembly of God in OT = <b>Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now Corinth = <b>everybody</b>, not just Jews</li><li class=\"d1\">maybe <b>not even predominantly</b> Jews</li></ul>"},{"t":116.06,"lv":3,"h":"Who they are: sanctified, holy ones","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Greeting = who they are, <b>or supposed to be</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people of God in Corinth - <b>not of Demeter</b>, but of the <b>Holy Trinity</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sanctified in Christ</b> = made holy, purified, <b>set apart</b> from everyone else in Corinth</li><li class=\"d1\">are they acting like it? \"<b>No</b>\" - but this is who they are in Christ</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Called to be saints</b> = <i>holy ones</i></li><li class=\"d1\">word used of <b>angels</b> in OT - the <b>divine counsel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">belong to Christ, <b>separate and special people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">called to <b>glorification</b> - <b>share in the life of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Every place</b> → part of something bigger, every Christian community in the world</li><li class=\"d0\">Reorients their thinking: addressing them as <b>who Christ created them to be</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hoping they <b>live up to</b> the calling</li></ul>"},{"t":275.28,"lv":2,"h":"Application: love people as who they should be","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Best way to show <b>love</b></li><li class=\"d0\">We treat people as we think they <b>deserve</b></li><li class=\"d1\">rude → treat as jerk; problem → treat as problem; like them → treat well</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's approach: <b>despite what they deserve</b>, treat them as <b>who they should be</b></li><li class=\"d1\">help them <b>rise to the occasion</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Because Paul <b>didn't get what he deserved</b> before Christ after <b>murdering Christians</b></li></ul>"},{"t":341.04,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: \"theirs and ours\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Does <i>both theirs and ours</i> refer to <b>Lord</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ours</b> = communities Paul was involved with; <b>theirs</b> = ones he <b>wasn't</b></li><li class=\"d0\">You're connected to <b>all of them</b>, whether Paul planted them or not</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this isn't the church of <b>Paul</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not the \"first <b>Pauline</b> church of Corinth\"</li></ul>"},{"t":393.36,"lv":2,"h":"1:3-9 - Grace, peace, enriched in Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:3</b>: \"Grace to you and peace from <b>God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul's normal way - Father and Christ <b>in tandem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">later in 1 Cor why that's important - where he gets the phrase (<b>tease</b>)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:4-9</b>: enriched in all utterance and knowledge; testimony confirmed; no gift lacking; waiting for the revelation; confirmed to the end, <b>blameless in the day</b>; <b>God is faithful</b>, called into <b>fellowship of his Son</b></li></ul>"},{"t":466.82,"lv":2,"h":"One sentence in Greek","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">All <b>one big sentence</b> in Greek</li><li class=\"d0\">English falls apart after a couple of clauses - <b>Greek, Latin, German</b> don't</li><li class=\"d1\">Caesar's <i>Gallic War</i> (Loeb): <b>17-page sentence</b>, last word is the <b>subject</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul gives him a <b>run for his money</b></li><li class=\"d1\">keeps latching on <b>clause after clause</b>, embedding them</li></ul>"},{"t":523.34,"lv":3,"h":"1:4-7 - Thanks for what was given","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul <b>constantly thanks God</b> for them</li><li class=\"d1\">not treating them as a <b>problem</b> - not that he doesn't know; he'll get to them</li><li class=\"d0\">Thanks for the <b>grace given</b>, not for <b>what they did with it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ reminding them: \"<b>you have everything you need</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Enriched in all utterance and knowledge</b> → taught the gospel, no <b>information</b> missing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Testimony of Christ confirmed in you</b> = gospel → likely their <b>baptism</b></li><li class=\"d1\">brought in <b>sacramentally</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Come short in no gift</b> → <b>gifts of the Holy Spirit</b> received</li></ul>"},{"t":631.91,"lv":2,"h":"\"Revelation\" - Christ never left","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Eagerly waiting for the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">English \"Christ's <b>return</b>\" - sounds like he <b>went away</b>, ascension = \"<b>balloon</b>\" floating off</li><li class=\"d1\">\"return\" implies he's <b>departed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Plays out in <b>Western theology</b> (oversimplification)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Roman Catholic</b>: Christ has a <b>vicar</b>, bishop of Rome; Peter left in charge</li><li class=\"d1\">most <b>Protestant</b>: Christ departed, <b>left a book</b> - \"until he returns, we've got the book\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Orthodox</b> and Paul: <b>Christ didn't go anywhere</b></li><li class=\"d1\">every liturgy: \"Christ is in our midst - <b>He is and ever shall be</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Eucharist</b> - he offers himself</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Matthew</b>: \"Lo, I am with you always, even until the end of the age\" → <b>not leaving</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's language: <b>revealed</b>, <b>glorious appearing</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><i>parousia</i> = <b>presence</b>, not return → \"when Christ is <b>present again</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">can't see and touch him <b>yet</b>, like the apostles</li></ul>"},{"t":845.54,"lv":3,"h":"Eagerly awaiting; blameless","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Revelation will bring <b>judgment</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ eagerly await = you <b>expect to be okay</b></li><li class=\"d1\">lived so that appearing = <b>blessed, rewarded, vindicated</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>don't dread it</b>; those working wickedness have to fear</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Confirm you to the end, blameless</b> - the goal: stand before him <b>blameless, pure</b></li><li class=\"d1\">back to the <b>holiness</b> language</li></ul>"},{"t":918.71,"lv":3,"h":"Day of our Lord = Yahweh; Trinity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Day of our Lord Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">prophets: <b>day of Yahweh</b> - God comes to visit his people, <b>reestablish justice</b>, judge the world</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul calls it the day of <b>Jesus</b> → \"<b>Jesus is Yahweh</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">already said <b>God (the Father)</b> and <b>Lord Jesus</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ <b>Holy Trinity</b> already in Paul's head - not \"come up with later\"</li><li class=\"d1\">speaks of them <b>separately</b>, identifies <b>both as Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So he can say, after identifying Christ as God: \"God is faithful, by whom you were called into fellowship of <b>his Son</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1029.2,"lv":2,"h":"1:10-12 - Divisions in the church","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:10</b>: \"Now I plead with you, <b>brethren</b>... speak the same thing, <b>no divisions</b>... same mind and judgment\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>brethren</b> - language for the faithful in each city (<b>Acts</b>) - family of God</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Now we get to the <b>bad news</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">heard of <b>factions, infighting</b> - \"never happens at our church\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Follows the pattern: opening <b>lays out themes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">who you are, what you've been given, what you're called to → \"<b>therefore</b>\" <b>one mind</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:11-12</b>: told by <b>Chloe's household</b> - \"there's the rat\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I am of <b>Paul</b>... <b>Apollos</b>... <b>Cephas</b> (Peter, Aramaic)... <b>Christ</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>fan clubs</b> around apostles/teachers</li><li class=\"d1\">the self-righteous: \"I'm of Christ\" to <b>trump</b> everybody</li></ul>"},{"t":1195.71,"lv":2,"h":"Aside; contemporary factions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Aside: age 6-7, Dutch, told friend family descended from <b>Japheth</b> - he said \"mine's descended from <b>Noah himself</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">same <b>one-upping</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Applies today</li><li class=\"d1\">Protestants: churches named for <b>Luther, Calvin, Wesley</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Orthodox too: <b>cults of personality</b> around teachers, personalities on <b>Ancient Faith Radio</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bicker online with <b>devotees</b> of the other</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: <b>destructive to the unity</b> of the church</li></ul>"},{"t":1320.53,"lv":2,"h":"1:13-16 - Is Christ divided?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:13</b>: \"Is <b>Christ divided</b>? Was <b>Paul crucified</b> for you? Were you <b>baptized in the name of Paul</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">obviously not → shouldn't be <b>my follower</b></li><li class=\"d1\">back to <b>1:1</b>: called and sent - important is <b>who called and sent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same for any priest or author: did they <b>die for you</b>? No</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:14-16</b>: thanks God he baptized only <b>Crispus and Gaius</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Paul doesn't have a good memory\" - also <b>household of Stephanas</b>, \"I don't know whether any other\"</li><li class=\"d1\">both <b>Roman names</b> → makeup of the Corinthian church</li><li class=\"d1\">so none could say baptized in <b>my own name</b></li><li class=\"d1\">imagine dictating: \"oh, also...\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1441.52,"lv":3,"h":"1:17 - Not to baptize but to preach","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:17</b>: \"Christ did not send me to baptize, but to <b>preach the gospel</b>, not with <b>wisdom of words</b>, lest the <b>cross</b> be made of no effect\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not sent to baptize and <b>form a group</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>John the Forerunner</b>'s baptizing in the Jordan = creating a <b>people of followers</b> for Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: gospel is about <b>Christ, not me</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not <b>brilliant rhetoric</b> - \"oh Paul, your sermons are so beautiful\"</li><li class=\"d1\">wanted focus on <b>Christ and his cross</b>, not <b>how wise</b> he was</li></ul>"},{"t":1526.63,"lv":2,"h":"1:18 - Message of the cross","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:18</b>: \"The message of the cross is <b>foolishness to those perishing</b>, but to us being saved it is the <b>power of God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">perishing = heading to <b>condemnation</b>, immersed in sins → <b>laugh</b>, \"ridiculous\" - as today</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Acts 17</b>: Athens - resurrection → <b>laughed out of the agora</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Saved = faithfully following Christ → <b>power of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">what's <b>changing your life</b>, gives all those gifts</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>message itself, Christ himself</b>, not how I preach it</li></ul>"},{"t":1607.31,"lv":2,"h":"1:19-21 - Wisdom of the world","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:19</b>: \"I will destroy the wisdom of the wise\" - <b>Isaiah 29</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:20-21</b>: \"Where is the wise? scribe? disputer?\" - world through wisdom <b>did not know God</b>; pleased God through <b>foolishness of the message</b> to save believers</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Gentile</b> audience - <b>wisdom prized</b>, <i>philosophia</i> = love of wisdom</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's <b>physical descriptions</b>: eyes oozing <b>pus</b>, <b>bald, short, bow-legged</b>, beaten nearly to death with <b>rocks, scourges</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"you would not find him <b>attractive</b>\" - \"I'm a fool, ridiculous\"</li><li class=\"d0\">→ the <b>message</b> brought you to know God, <b>not him</b>; proves it's <b>God himself</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Does the foolishness refer to the message - <b>resurrection</b> as nonsense?</li><li class=\"d1\">get to that - here he's talking about the <b>cross</b> specifically</li></ul>"},{"t":1773.72,"lv":2,"h":"1:22-25 - Sign and wisdom","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:22</b>: \"<b>Jews request a sign</b>, Greeks seek <b>wisdom</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Jews want <b>miracles</b> - <b>John's gospel</b>: \"show us something new\", never enough</li><li class=\"d1\">Greeks: <b>philosophical arguments</b>, speculation, lofty discourse</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>But we preach Christ crucified</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God became a \"<b>less than dirt poor peasant</b>\", executed in humiliating way by <b>Romans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a display of power, not lofty argument</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Stumbling block to Jews</b>: Romans crucified would-be <b>Messiahs</b> → sign you weren't</li></ul>"},{"t":1878.63,"lv":3,"h":"Foolishness to Greeks","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Greek gods = <b>power</b>; \"you <b>become like what you worship</b>\" - true principle</li><li class=\"d1\">Zeus = power; <b>beauty, sensuality, wealth, strength, health, harvest</b></li><li class=\"d1\">show them <b>Jesus executed on a cross</b> - \"what?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Graffiti</b> (late 1st / early 2nd c.): Romans mocking a Christian soldier</li><li class=\"d1\">man with <b>donkey head</b> crucified; man kneeling: \"so-and-so worshiping his God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">→ \"you want to become like <b>that</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:24-25</b>: to the called, Jews and Greeks, <b>Christ the power and wisdom of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>foolishness of God wiser than men</b>, weakness stronger</li><li class=\"d0\">Both the message and the <b>person who came preaching it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">didn't give people what they <b>wanted</b> - gave <b>what they needed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">refocus on <b>Christ who offered his life for the life of the world</b>, not \"I'm this guy's fan\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2058.07,"lv":2,"h":"1:26-29 - Look at your calling","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:26</b>: \"For you see your calling, brethren\" - <b>called</b>, the verb he used for himself</li><li class=\"d1\">not same mission, but still <b>called</b></li><li class=\"d1\">look around at the gathering: <b>not many wise, mighty, noble</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:27-29</b>: God chose the <b>foolish</b> to shame the wise, <b>weak</b> to shame the mighty, <b>base and despised</b>, \"things which are <b>not</b>\" to bring to nothing \"things that are\"</li><li class=\"d1\">one big sentence</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul <b>includes himself</b> - \"that includes you, that includes me\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>No flesh should glory</b> in his presence</li></ul>"},{"t":2173.79,"lv":3,"h":"\"Things which are not\" - God's name","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Reference to <b>God's name</b>; Paul <b>speaks historically</b> (as in Romans)</li><li class=\"d1\">God has always worked this way - <b>Yahweh vs. pagan gods</b> of strength, wealth, beauty</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Torah</b>: God identifies with <b>nomads, orphans, widows, poor, strangers, slaves in Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>Pharaoh</b> laughs: \"God of a bunch of slaves?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">being his people = being like that</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Yahweh</b> = form of Hebrew verb <b>to be</b>, <b>Hiphil</b> (causative) → \"<b>he who causes things to be</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Hebrew verbs: no tenses, <b>binyanim</b></li><li class=\"d1\">creator - and brought <b>Israel</b> into being, not a nation: slaves, refugees, nomads, <b>not all descended from Jacob</b> (Exodus later)</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul in Romans: <b>church</b> = Gentiles, Jews, Greeks made <b>one people</b></li><li class=\"d0\">He <b>takes things that aren't, makes them something</b> - doing it with the Corinthians</li><li class=\"d0\">God identifies with the lowly so <b>no one can be proud</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Paul's not here for <b>my glory</b>; you shouldn't be\" - \"we're the <b>dregs</b>, despised, mocked\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God now does <b>powerful things among us</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2436.06,"lv":2,"h":"1:30-31 - Christ our wisdom, righteousness, sanctification, redemption","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:30-31</b>: \"of him you are in Christ Jesus, who became for us <b>wisdom from God, righteousness, sanctification, redemption</b>... he who glories, let him glory in the <b>Lord</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">wisdom - want it, <b>Greeks</b>? need <b>Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">righteousness - <b>Pharisees</b>? Christ is God's righteousness</li><li class=\"d1\">sanctification - want to be <b>holy</b>? Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">redemption = <b>forgiveness of sins</b>, bought back, purchased back from sin</li><li class=\"d0\">→ boast about <b>Christ</b>, not <b>Paul, Apollos, Peter</b></li><li class=\"d0\">End of <b>chapter 1</b></li></ul>"}]});
